1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,694
The pressure built after a lengthy morning in court.

2
00:00:02,694 --> 00:00:11,028
The council had moved the hearing twice, and the township had offered one more decade of patience and no more money.

3
00:00:11,028 --> 00:00:19,167
May and June had gone; maybe the offer would come in September, and perhaps it would not come at all.

4
00:00:19,167 --> 00:00:30,246
Since the outset, the team had promised one thing: they would remain until the service was efficient or until it was clear that it could not be.

5
00:00:30,246 --> 00:00:36,820
A pessimistic councillor supposed that the whole exercise was a pastime for students.

6
00:00:36,820 --> 00:00:42,905
“I refuse to praise a report that refuses to name a price,” he said.

7
00:00:42,905 --> 00:00:53,854
“You deserve the applause you get, and no more.” The rejection was brief and utter, and the applause that followed it was for him.

8
00:00:53,854 --> 00:00:58,118
The gratitude of the travellers was harder to dismiss.

9
00:00:58,118 --> 00:01:10,837
A trader in illegal trafficking had been confined for a month; a hateful landlord had raised the rent of the inn; a contemptible clause in the contract had been signed repeatedly.

10
00:01:10,837 --> 00:01:17,381
“A worthwhile project is one that survives its own bad decade,” Aisha said.

11
00:01:17,381 --> 00:01:20,781
“We are presently in it.”

12
00:01:20,781 --> 00:01:29,740
They would finally interact with the council through a single document, and they would maintain one copy of it in the local language.

13
00:01:29,740 --> 00:01:33,745
“I bet they postpone the vote,” Lin wrote.

14
00:01:33,745 --> 00:01:46,638
“I bet they resign the question instead.” The lump in his throat was not fear; it was the thank you he had not said to his father, who had died that spring.

15
00:01:46,638 --> 00:01:51,123
The eventual answer arrived shortly before the election.

16
00:01:51,123 --> 00:01:58,312
It was not a marvel, and it was not admirable; it was a permission with three conditions.

17
00:01:58,312 --> 00:02:02,801
“Be thankful for the small ones,” Maya said.

18
00:02:02,801 --> 00:02:11,880
“Forever is not our business.” The group applauded once, quietly, and went back to work on the timetable.

19
00:02:11,880 --> 00:02:19,414
Across the day and the court, the council moved once more, and the offer remained possible.

20
00:02:19,414 --> 00:02:24,164
“Maybe we go, perhaps we stay,” Lin wrote.

21
00:02:24,164 --> 00:02:39,967
“One thing is certain: the permission has been ours only since May.” They had to maintain the service for a decade, to praise nothing they had not seen, and to thank the clerk who had lost her own job to help them.

22
00:02:39,967 --> 00:02:58,005
A century of habit was harder to reject than a clause; eventually they would pray for a better vote, contend with the popularity of the old route, and ask whether a confinement of one month could ever be justified when the alternative was nothing.
